      en: "Place du Palais is the central square in front of the Prince's Palace of Monaco. It offers stunning views of the Mediterranean Sea and the port. The square was laid out in the 13th century and is the setting for the famous changing of the guard. It is surrounded by historic buildings, including the palace chapel. The square is about 2,000 m² and paved with stone slabs. State ceremonies and concerts take place here. The viewpoint terrace is very popular with tourists. The square is a symbol of the monarchy.",
